Here’s the frontend-side trace for the Course Management edit flow when changing fixed weekdays like Monday/Tuesday/Thursday.

## 1) Files / components / composables involved

Primary edit flow:
- `frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue`
- `frontend/src/components/CourseEditForm.vue`

Supporting schedule/session display logic:
- `frontend/src/composables/course-management/useCourseSessionsDisplay.js`

Related but not the main edit-save path:
- `frontend/src/composables/course-management/useSessionEditFlow.js`
- `frontend/src/components/UniversalClassScheduler.vue`
- `frontend/src/lib/universalSchedulerApi.js`
- `frontend/src/lib/sessionDates.js`

What each one does:
- `CourseManagement.vue` opens the edit modal, seeds `editForm`, decides whether to use the Laravel `PUT /api/v1/student-classes/{id}` path, and builds the save payload.
- `CourseEditForm.vue` is where weekdays are actually collected via chips/checkboxes and synchronized with `day_time_slots`.
- `useCourseSessionsDisplay.js` affects what the user sees after save, including the “堂次偏移” badge and how duplicate/conflicting session rows are interpreted.
- `UniversalClassScheduler.vue` is mostly for create/backfill, but it uses the same domain concepts: `days_of_week`, `day_time_slots`, `session_plan`, fixed weekday validation, and schedule protections.

A key save-path snippet is here:

```2245:2347:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
const submitEdit = async () => {
  const id = editingId.value;
  const form = editForm.value;
  if (editingCourseFromLaravel.value) {
    ...
    const body = {
      ...
      days_of_week: (form.days_of_week || []).length ? form.days_of_week : [],
      start_time: form.start_time,
      day_time_slots: (form.day_time_slots || [])
        .map((slot) => ({
          day: Number(slot?.day || 0),
          start_time: normalizeTo30Min(slot?.start_time || form.start_time || '16:00'),
          duration_minutes: Number(slot?.duration_hours || 0) > 0 ? Math.round(Number(slot.duration_hours) * 60) : undefined,
        }))
        .filter((slot) => slot.day >= 1 && slot.day <= 7),
      ...
      force_rebuild_if_mismatch: true,
      ...
    };
    const res = await fetch(`/api/v1/student-classes/${id}`, { method: 'PUT', ... });
    ...
    const scheduleChanged = baseline != null && scheduleFingerprintForEdit(form) !== baseline;
    if (scheduleChanged) {
      const rbRes = await fetch(`/api/v1/student-classes/${id}`, {
        method: 'PUT',
        ...
        body: JSON.stringify({ force_partial_rebuild: true }),
      });
    }
```

## 2) How weekday values are collected and sent

### In the edit modal
`CourseEditForm.vue` collects weekday selection from `form.days_of_week` and then keeps `form.day_time_slots` in sync.

Relevant code:

```92:157:frontend/src/components/CourseEditForm.vue
<div class="form-group span-full">
  <label>固定排課日（可多選）</label>
  <div class="day-checkbox-group">
    <label
      v-for="d in dayOptions"
      :key="d.value"
      :class="['day-chip', { selected: selectedDaySet.has(d.value) }]"
    >
      <input
        type="checkbox"
        :value="d.value"
        v-model="form.days_of_week"
        ...
      />
      {{ d.label }}
    </label>
  </div>
  <div v-if="(form.days_of_week || []).length > 0" class="day-time-slots">
    <div
      v-for="(slot, idx) in (form.day_time_slots || [])"
      ...
    >
      ...
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Sync behavior inside the form
This component is doing a lot of protection work:
- normalizes weekday values to numbers `1..7`
- derives `selectedDaySet`
- auto-adds/removes `day_time_slots` when weekday chips change
- restores weekday chips from existing `day_time_slots` if the parent payload only had slots
- emits a normalized payload upward

The most important watcher is:

```264:344:frontend/src/components/CourseEditForm.vue
watch(
  () => form.days_of_week,
  () => {
    if (syncingFromParent) return;
    syncDayTimeSlotsFromSelection();
  },
  { deep: true }
);

watch(
  form,
  () => {
    if (syncingFromParent) return;
    const payload = {
      ...form,
      rate_unit: hasPerDayDuration.value ? 'hour' : (form.rate_unit || 'session'),
      days_of_week: sortedSelectedDays.value,
      day_time_slots: [...(form.day_time_slots || [])].map((slot) => ({
        day: Number(slot?.day || 0),
        start_time: String(slot?.start_time || '').slice(0, 5),
        duration_hours: Number(slot?.duration_hours || 0) || undefined,
        duration_minutes: Number(slot?.duration_hours || 0) > 0 ? Math.round(Number(slot.duration_hours) * 60) : undefined,
      })),
    };
    emit('update:modelValue', payload);
  },
  { deep: true }
);
```

And the actual weekday-to-slot reconciliation:

```306:344:frontend/src/components/CourseEditForm.vue
function syncDayTimeSlotsFromSelection() {
  let chipDays = new Set(
    [...new Set((form.days_of_week || []).map((d) => Number(d)).filter((d) => d >= 1 && d <= 7))]
  );
  let slots = [...(form.day_time_slots || [])];

  if (chipDays.size === 0 && slots.length > 0 && syncingFromParent) {
    form.days_of_week = [...new Set(slots.map((s) => Number(s?.day || 0)).filter((d) => d >= 1 && d <= 7))].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    chipDays = new Set(form.days_of_week);
  }

  if (syncingFromParent && slots.length > 0) {
    const fromSlots = [...new Set(slots.map((s) => Number(s?.day || 0)).filter((d) => d >= 1 && d <= 7))].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    form.days_of_week = fromSlots;
    chipDays = new Set(fromSlots);
  }

  if (chipDays.size > 0) {
    slots = slots.filter((s) => chipDays.has(Number(s?.day || 0)));
  } else if (!syncingFromParent) {
    slots = [];
  }

  ...
  for (const day of [...chipDays].sort((a, b) => a - b)) {
    if (!slots.some((s) => Number(s.day) === day)) {
      slots.push({ day, start_time: baseTime, duration_hours: dur });
    }
  }
  form.day_time_slots = slots;
}
```

### In `CourseManagement.vue`
When the user clicks edit, the page seeds the form from the course row:

```2192:2242:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
const editCourse = (c) => {
  ...
  const existingDaysRaw = Array.isArray(c.days_of_week) && c.days_of_week.length
    ? c.days_of_week.map(Number).filter((d) => d >= 1 && d <= 7)
    : (c.day_of_week ? [Number(c.day_of_week)] : []);

  const existingSlots = Array.isArray(c.day_time_slots)
    ? c.day_time_slots
        .map((slot) => ({
          day: Number(slot?.day || 0),
          start_time: normalizeTo30Min(slot?.start_time || c.start_time || '16:00'),
          duration_hours: Number(slot?.duration_hours || 0) || c.duration_hours || 2,
        }))
        .filter((slot) => slot.day >= 1 && slot.day <= 7)
    : [];

  const slotDays = existingSlots.map((s) => s.day).filter((d) => d >= 1 && d <= 7);
  const existingDays = [...new Set([...existingDaysRaw, ...slotDays])].sort((a, b) => a - b);

  editForm.value = {
    ...
    days_of_week: existingDays,
    day_time_slots: existingSlots,
    ...
  };
  ...
};
```

Then on save, the Laravel path sends both:
- `days_of_week`
- `day_time_slots` as `{ day, start_time, duration_minutes }[]`

It also computes a schedule fingerprint based on:
- selected weekdays
- normalized slot rows
- duration
- start time
- first class date

That fingerprint determines whether a second `force_partial_rebuild` call is made.

```2171:2189:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
function scheduleFingerprintForEdit(form) {
  const days = [...new Set((f.days_of_week || []).map(Number).filter((d) => d >= 1 && d <= 7))]
    .sort((a, b) => a - b)
    .join(',');
  const slotRows = (f.day_time_slots || [])
    .map((s) => ({
      day: Number(s?.day || 0),
      start: normalizeTo30Min(String(s?.start_time || f.start_time || '16:00').slice(0, 5)),
      dur: Math.round((Number(s?.duration_hours || 0) || Number(f.duration_hours) || 2) * 10) / 10,
    }))
    .filter((s) => s.day >= 1 && s.day <= 7)
    .sort((a, b) => a.day - b.day || a.start.localeCompare(b.start) || a.dur - b.dur);
  ...
}
```

## 3) Likely frontend-side causes if save appears ineffective

These are the strongest frontend-side suspects.

### A. Wrong save branch: Laravel course misdetected as non-Laravel
`CourseManagement.vue` does not always use the Laravel `PUT` path. It first decides via `editingCourseFromLaravel`.

If that heuristic fails, it uses the legacy Supabase update path instead, which only writes:
- `days_of_week`
- `start_time`
- `end_time`
- a few basic fields

It does **not** send `day_time_slots` and does **not** trigger the rebuild logic.

```2193:2199:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
editingCourseFromLaravel.value = !!(
  c.data_source === 'laravel'
  || c.branch_name != null
  || c.room_name != null
  || c.settlement_day != null
);
```

Legacy fallback:

```2360:2374:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
const { error } = await supabase.from('student-classes').update({
  ...
  days_of_week: form.days_of_week,
  start_time: form.start_time,
  end_time: endTime,
  ...
}).eq('id', id);
```

Why this matters:
- if a real Laravel-backed course gets classified into the Supabase path, weekday edits may look partially ignored
- multi-slot/per-day info is dropped
- no `force_partial_rebuild`
- no session sync feedback

For a “change to Monday/Tuesday/Thursday” complaint, this is one of the best frontend explanations.

### B. User changes weekdays, but visible list is still showing stale contract/session data until reload
After success, the code calls `loadCourses()` but does not `await` it before returning control to the user.

```2345:2347:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
showEditModal.value = false;
alert(successMsg);
loadCourses();
```

If reload is slow or another data source is stale, the user can briefly see old weekdays and think save did nothing.

### C. The edit modal starts from stale `c.day_time_slots` / `c.days_of_week`
The modal seeds from the course row currently in memory, not from a fresh detail fetch. If the row itself is stale, the modal starts stale too. The code is careful, but still depends on whatever `loadCourses()` last returned.

### D. Backend accepted `days_of_week`, but returned/kept old `day_time_slots`; UI may appear unchanged
The page’s preferred contract display is `day_time_slots`, not raw `days_of_week`:

```1736:1757:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
const formatDayTimeSlotLines = (course) => {
  const slots = Array.isArray(course?.day_time_slots) ? course.day_time_slots : [];
  ...
};
```

So if the save only updates `days_of_week` but not the returned `day_time_slots`, the display can still look old. That’s partly backend-shaped, but from the frontend symptom perspective it’s important: the visible label depends heavily on `day_time_slots`.

### E. Schedule changed, but second rebuild call failed
The frontend does a second `PUT` with `{ force_partial_rebuild: true }` only when the fingerprint changes. If that rebuild fails, the code still reports the course update as successful, with a warning appended.

That means the contract may save, but future session rows may remain on old weekdays/times, which can make the page look inconsistent.

```2293:2306:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
if (scheduleChanged) {
  const rbRes = await fetch(`/api/v1/student-classes/${id}`, {
    method: 'PUT',
    ...
    body: JSON.stringify({ force_partial_rebuild: true }),
  });
  ...
}
```

### F. If only weekday chips changed but `day_time_slots` got out of sync, save body may not match user intent
`CourseEditForm.vue` tries hard to prevent this, but the save body ultimately sends both arrays. If something external mutates the form unexpectedly, the saved truth is really the normalized `day_time_slots` plus `days_of_week`, not just the visible chip state.

That said, the form code includes good guards, so this is less likely than A or E.

## 4) Regression protections already present

There are several explicit protections already in the frontend and docs.

### Protection 1: `CourseEditForm` keeps weekday chips and slot rows consistent
This is the biggest frontend guard:
- if weekdays are unchecked, corresponding slots are removed
- if slots exist but weekdays are missing from parent data, weekdays are restored from slots
- when loading from parent, slots are treated as canonical if present
- emitted payload is normalized to numeric weekday values

That directly protects against “chips say one thing, payload says another.”

### Protection 2: Save path fingerprints schedule changes and auto-triggers partial rebuild
`CourseManagement.vue` stores a baseline fingerprint when the edit modal opens, then compares it on save. If changed, it automatically issues a rebuild request.

This is explicitly intended to keep future unsent sessions aligned after weekday changes.

### Protection 3: UI shows “堂次偏移” instead of silently hiding drift
The course list can show a schedule-drift badge telling the user that contract weekdays/times and future session rows are out of sync.

```178:186:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
<span v-else-if="(c.days_of_week || []).length > 0">
  {{ (c.days_of_week || []).map(d => dayLabel(d)).join('、') }} {{ c.start_time }}~{{ c.end_time }}
</span>
...
<span v-if="c.schedule_drift" class="schedule-drift-badge" ...>⚠ 堂次偏移</span>
```

That’s a strong regression defense against “save looked fine but future rows are still old.”

### Protection 4: Contract display prefers `day_time_slots`
The UI comment is explicit: display uses contract `day_time_slots`, not inferred session history.

```1736:1737:frontend/src/pages/CourseManagement.vue
/** 每段一行（同日多時段會多行），供「時段」欄位顯示；以契約 day_time_slots 為準 */
```

That is consistent with the regression doc warning not to let historical `ClassSession` data overwrite the contract.

### Protection 5: Regression docs explicitly cover weekday-edit sync
The strongest written protection is in `docs/AI_REGRESSION_LESSONS.md`, especially this section:

```382:386:docs/AI_REGRESSION_LESSONS.md
| **曾發生的錯誤** | **(A)** `UniversalClassScheduler.vue` 組 `session_plan` 時，若使用者點選的日曆日之星期幾**未**在 `day_time_slots`／`days_of_week` 內... |
| **正確行為** | ... `StudentClassController::index`：課程主檔 `week*`／`time*` 組出的時段為**契約** ...
| **禁止回歸** | **(a)** 勿恢復 `session_plan` 的錯誤日曆日 fallback。 ... **(d)** 勿把 `syncFutureScheduledSessionTimes` 改回「只改 Start/End、遇到契約外星期就略過」而讓未來堂永遠卡在舊星期。 |
| **關聯檔案** | **前端**：`frontend/src/components/UniversalClassScheduler.vue` ... **後端**：`StudentClassController.php` ...
| **測試** | `StudentClassUpdateScheduleReconcileTest::test_update_weekday_remaps_future_sessions_from_saturday_to_sunday` |
```

And this one is also directly relevant:

```310:314:docs/AI_REGRESSION_LESSONS.md
| **曾發生的錯誤** | ... 前端 `editCourse` 從 `classSessionsByCourse` 合併推斷時段至 `existingSlots`，同樣污染固定排課。 ...
| **正確行為** | ... `editCourse` 與 `formatDayTimeSlotLines` 只使用契約資料，不從堂次合併。 ...
| **禁止回歸** | ... 勿在前端 `editCourse` 或 `formatDayTimeSlotLines` 中用堂次資料覆寫契約 slots。 |
```

That matches the current `editCourse()` implementation: it seeds from `c.day_time_slots` / `c.days_of_week`, not from session rows.

## Bottom line

The current frontend edit flow is:

1. `CourseManagement.vue` opens `CourseEditForm`.
2. `CourseEditForm.vue` collects weekday chips into `days_of_week` and auto-syncs `day_time_slots`.
3. `submitEdit()` sends both arrays to `PUT /api/v1/student-classes/{id}`.
4. If the schedule fingerprint changed, frontend immediately sends a second `PUT` with `force_partial_rebuild: true` to realign future unsent sessions.

If changing weekdays to Monday/Tuesday/Thursday “saves but looks ineffective,” the most likely frontend causes are:
- the course took the legacy non-Laravel save branch due to `editingCourseFromLaravel` heuristic misclassification
- the visible row is stale immediately after save because reload is not awaited
- the backend kept/returned old `day_time_slots`, and the frontend display prefers `day_time_slots`
- the second rebuild call failed, so contract changed but future session rows still reflect old weekdays

